Now I understand the test framework better. The tests are using happy-dom, not a real browser. The issue is that the Cypress acceptance test runs in a real browser.

Looking at the test step for toggling:
```javascript
When('I click the toggle for todo at index {int}', function (index) {
  const todo = getTodo(this.document, index);
  const toggle = todo.querySelector('.toggle');
  clickEl(this.window, toggle);
});
```

This dispatches a click event directly on the toggle element. Then the app handles it in the `toggle()` function.

The issue in a real browser (Cypress) is likely that after clicking, Cypress tries to chain commands on the element, but the DOM has been updated in a way that detaches the element.

